ing these CONFIGS.md rows (read `translation/CONFIGS.md`):\n- row 11: push each of the 7 value kinds, then js_type + js_typeof + all js_is* predicates on each (cross product; print a matrix)\n- row 13: js_pushstring / js_pushlstring / js_pushliteral with short (<=8 bytes), long, empty, UTF-8, embedded NUL via lstring, n=0, n truncating mid-UTF-8; then js_tostring, js_isstring, js_utflen of the result\n- row 14: js_toboolean / js_tonumber / js_tostring over the cross product of all value kinds (incl. objects with custom valueOf/toString created via js_dostring + js_getglobal)\n- row 21: js_trystring / js_trynumber / js_tryinteger / js_tryboolean / js_tryrepr on coercible values, on undefined/null, and on an object whose toString/valueOf throws\n- row 22: js_compare (both the return value and the `okay` out-parameter) for number/number, string/string, mixed, NaN, objects — randomized numbers and strings too\n- row 23: js_equal and js_strictequal over the cross product of value kinds incl. NaN, +0/-0, \"1\" vs 1, null vs undefined\n- row 24: js_instanceof — matching prototype, non-matching, non-object right-hand side (that one throws: it is fine as long as both libraries behave identically; wrap via js_dostring or accept the abort/exception equally)\n- row 25: js_concat for string+string, number+number, string+object, object+object, empty strings, long strings\n- row 26: js_repr / js_torepr / js_tryrepr for all value kinds, nested arrays/objects, cyclic object\n- row 27: js_pop, js_rot, js_copy, js_remove, js_insert, js_replace with positive AND negative indices; after each op print js_gettop and js_tostring/js_typeof of every stack slot\n- row 28: js_dup, js_dup2, js_rot2, js_rot3, js_rot4, js_rot2pop1, js_rot3pop2 — same style of full stack dump after each\n- row 85 (partial): js_tovalue + js_pushvalue round-trip, js_pushobject with an object obtained from js_toobject, jsV_newmemstring + printing via the value\n- row 86: js_toprimitive / jsV_toprimitive with hint 0, 1, 2 AND an out-of-range hint (e.g. 99) on objects with valueOf/toString\n- row 87: jsV_toboolean / jsV_tonumber / jsV_tointeger / jsV_tostring / jsV_toobject via `js_tovalue` pointers over all value kinds\n- row 88: js_toobject on each primitive, and js_isarrayindex for \"0\", \"1\", \"-1\", \"01\", \"4294967295\", \"4294967294\", \"\", \"abc\", \"1e2\", \" 1\", \"0x10\", huge numeric strings (print return value AND the out idx)\n\nHelper you will need: to build objects with custom valueOf/toString, run a script with js_dostring (e.g. `var o = {valueOf: function(){return 42}}`) then `js_getglobal(J, cs(\"o\").as_ptr())`.\n\nWrite one `#[test] fn` per row named `cfg11_...`, `cfg13_...`, etc.\n\nVerify with: `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-dNzXE1/translation && timeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test values -- --test-threads=1 2>&1 | tail -60`\n\nIf a test reveals a DIVERGENCE between the C and Rust libraries, do NOT fix translation/src — keep the failing test and report the exact divergence.\n\nFINAL REPORT (concise): each test fn, pass/fail, and for failures the exact diverging lines/status.","uuid":"73674e90-30e2-4e8f-9e3d-1c5fc44a2394","session_id":"5c8219bc-b0e9-40a9-995a-ed544487508c"}
