tive; then loop js_nextiterator printing each key\n- 42: low-level jsV_newiterator(J, obj, own) + jsV_nextiterator for the same shapes\n- 43: js_getglobal / js_setglobal / js_defglobal (atts 0..7) / js_delglobal for existing built-ins (\"print\"? \"Object\", \"Math\"), new names, and missing names; print js_typeof of what you read back\n- 44: js_setregistry / js_getregistry / js_delregistry: set/get/delete/missing key, overwrite, empty-string key\n- 45: js_ref / js_unref: ref several values (numbers, strings, objects), print the returned ref strings, read them back through js_getregistry, unref, then read again\n- 51: js_newboolean / js_newnumber / js_newstring wrapper objects + js_isbooleanobject / js_isnumberobject / js_isstringobject / js_isdateobject / js_toboolean / js_tonumber / js_tostring on each\n- 52: js_newerror + js_newevalerror + js_newrangeerror + js_newreferenceerror + js_newsyntaxerror + js_newtypeerror + js_newurierror; for each print js_iserror, js_typeof, js_tostring, and the \"name\"/\"message\"/\"stack\" properties (skip \"stack\" if it embeds file paths/line numbers that could differ — check by running it)\n\nWrite one `#[test] fn` per row: `cfg29_...` ... `cfg45_...`, `cfg51_...`, `cfg52_...`.\n\nVerify with: `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-dNzXE1/translation && timeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test objects -- --test-threads=1 2>&1 | tail -60`\n\nIf a test reveals a DIVERGENCE, do NOT fix translation/src — keep the failing test and report the exact divergence.\n\nFINAL REPORT (concise): each test fn, pass/fail, and for failures the exact diverging lines/status.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-8cjUpj/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-dNzXE1/5c8219bc-b0e9-40a9-995a-ed544487508c/tasks/a04006e9c03ae461f.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
