tes, decoded rune, decode length) into a running 64-bit FNV checksum; print the checksum every 0x10000 runes AND print full detail lines for the first 300 runes, for runes 0x7F..0x81, 0x7FF..0x801, 0xD7FF..0xE001, 0xFFFD..0x10002, 0x10FFFE..0x110002. Print the final checksum. A checksum divergence localises to a 64K block; that is acceptable.\n- row 72b: jsU_chartorune on INVALID/truncated UTF-8 byte sequences: every single byte 0x00..0xFF as a 1-byte string, all 2-byte sequences starting with 0xC0..0xFF followed by 0x00/0x41/0x80/0xBF/0xFF, overlong encodings (C0 80, E0 80 80, F0 80 80 80), surrogate encodings (ED A0 80, ED BF BF), 5- and 6-byte lead bytes (F8..FF), and truncated multibyte sequences at end of string. Print the returned length and rune for each.\n- row 73: jsU_isalpharune / islowerrune / isupperrune / tolowerrune / toupperrune for every rune 0..=0x11000: same checksum strategy, but ALSO print a full detail line for every rune where isalpha/islower/isupper is non-zero OR tolower(c)!=c OR toupper(c)!=c AND the rune is < 0x600 (keeps the exhaustive detail bounded); checksum the rest. Print the final checksum. Include the negative/huge inputs too.\n- row 74: jsU_tolowerrune_full / jsU_toupperrune_full over every rune 0..=0x2000 plus the known multi-char cases (0xDF, 0x130, 0x1F0, 0x149, 0x390, 0x587, 0xFB00..0xFB17, 0x1E96..0x1E9A, 0x1F50, 0x1F80..0x1FFF where applicable) — print the full returned sequence for every rune whose sequence length != 1 or whose single element != the plain tolower/toupper result; checksum everything else.\n- row 75: js_utflen / js_utfptrtoidx / js_runeat over a corpus of strings: \"\", \"a\", \"abc\", \"héllo\", \"日本語\", a string with a 4-byte emoji, strings with invalid UTF-8 bytes (0xFF, 0xC0 0x41, 0xE0 0x80), a string with an embedded 0x80 continuation byte, and 200 random byte strings (fixed-seed Rng, bytes 1..=0xFF, length 1..16, NUL-terminated). For js_utfptrtoidx pass pointers at every byte offset within the string (pr