xisting const asserts or as runtime checks — behaviour is identical either way)\n\nWhat to do: in each corresponding Rust function, at exactly the same point in the control flow as the C assert, add a check that calls libc `abort()` when the condition is false. Follow the crate conventions in `translation/GUIDE.md`... (it is at /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-dNzXE1/GUIDE.md): no Rust std allocation, no println!, use the libc bindings already declared in `translation/src/jsi.rs` (add your own `extern \"C\" { fn abort() -> !; }` block at the top of the file if `abort` is not already declared there — check first: `grep -n \"abort\" translation/src/jsi.rs`).\n\nDo NOT print anything before aborting: the C `__assert_fail` message contains the C source path and the program name, which can never match, and the differential harness compares only the captured output plus the exit status. Just `abort()`.\n\nDo not change any other behaviour or reorder any code.\n\nThen verify:\n1. `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-dNzXE1/translation && timeout 600 cargo build --release --offline 2>&1 | tail -20` (must build clean)\n2. `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-dNzXE1/dtest && gcc -O1 -I../c_src/include -o driver_r driver.c ../translation/target/release/libmujs.so -lm -Wl,-rpath,'$ORIGIN/../translation/target/release' && ./driver_r -lowlevel > /dev/null 2>&1; echo \"rust exit: $?\"; ./driver_c -lowlevel > /dev/null 2>&1; echo \"c exit: $?\"` — both must report the same exit code (134 / signal 6), and the stdout produced before the abort must match: `./driver_c -lowlevel 2>/dev/null | md5sum; ./driver_r -lowlevel 2>/dev/null | md5sum` must be equal.\n3. Confirm the number of exported symbols is unchanged: `nm -D --defined-only translation/target/release/libmujs.so | awk '$2==\"T\"' | wc -l` must still be 237.\n\nReport: the exact edits you made (file + function + condition), and the verification output for steps 1-3."}}],"stop_reason"