") {\n413\t        return PathBuf::from(p);\n414\t    }\n415\t    let base = PathBuf::from(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")).join(\"target\");\n416\t    let rel = base.join(\"release/libmujs.so\");\n417\t    let dbg = base.join(\"debug/libmujs.so\");\n418\t    match (rel.exists(), dbg.exists()) {\n419\t        (true, true) => {\n420\t            let mr = std::fs::metadata(&rel).unwrap().modified().unwrap();\n421\t            let md = std::fs::metadata(&dbg).unwrap().modified().unwrap();\n422\t            if md > mr { dbg } else { rel }\n423\t        }\n424\t        (true, false) => rel,\n425\t        (false, true) => dbg,\n426\t        _ => panic!(\"no Rust libmujs.so built\"),\n427\t    }\n428\t}\n429\t\n430\tfn c_so() -> PathBuf {\n431\t    if let Ok(p) = std::env::var(\"MUJS_C_SO\") {\n432\t        return PathBuf::from(p);\n433\t    }\n434\t    root().join(\"c_src/build/libmujs.so\")\n435\t}\n436\t\n437\tpub fn libs() -> &'static Libs {\n438\t    LIBS.get_or_init(|| unsafe {\n439\t        let cpath = c_so();\n440\t        let rpath = rust_so();\n441\t        assert!(cpath.exists(), \"missing {}\", cpath.display());\n442\t        assert!(rpath.exists(), \"missing {}\", rpath.display());\n443\t        /* The C library is linked without -lm (see c_src/CMakeLists.txt), so\n444\t         * pull libm into the global scope first. */\n445\t        let libm = libloading::os::unix::Library::open(\n446\t            Some(\"libm.so.6\"),\n447\t            libloading::os::unix::RTLD_NOW | libloading::os::unix::RTLD_GLOBAL,\n448\t        );\n449\t        std::mem::forget(libm);\n450\t        let cl = libloading::Library::new(&cpath).expect(\"dlopen C lib\");\n451\t        let rl = libloading::Library::new(&rpath).expect(\"dlopen Rust lib\");\n452\t        let c = Api::build(&cl, \"C\");\n453\t        let r = Api::build(&rl, \"RUST\");\n454\t        Libs { c, r, _libs: (cl, rl) }\n455\t    })\n456\t}\n457\t\n458\t/* --- libc bits used by the harness --------------------------------------- */\n459\t\n460\textern \"C\" {\n461\t    fn fork() -> c_int;\n462\t    fn waitpid(pid: c_int, status: *mut c_int, options: c_int) -> c_int;\n463\t    fn _exit(code: c_int) -> !;\n464\t    fn dup2(old: c_int, new: c_int) -> c_int;\n465\t    fn open(path: *const c_char, flags: c_int, ...) -> c_int;\n466\t    fn close(fd: c_int) -> c_int;\n467\t    fn fflush(f: *mut c_void) -> c_int;\n468\t    fn printf(fmt: *const c_char, ...) -> c_int;\n469\t    fn putchar(c: c_int) -> c_int;\n470\t    fn fputs(s: *const c_char, f: *mut c_void) -> c_int;\n471\t    fn puts(s: *const c_char) -> c_int;\n472\t    fn strlen(s: *const c_char) -> usize;\n473\t}\n474\t\n475\tconst O_RDWR: c_int = 2;\n476\tconst O_CREAT: c_int = 64;\n477\tconst O_TRUNC: c_int = 512;\n478\t\n479\t/// Run `f` in a forked child with stdout+stderr redirected to a temp file.\n480\t/// Returns the captured bytes and the raw wait status.\n481\tpub fn capture<F: FnOnce()>(tag: &str, f: F) -> (Vec<u8>, c_int) {\n482\t    let dir = std::env::temp_dir();\n483\t    let path = dir.join(format!(\n484\t        \"mujs_diff_{}_{}_{}.out\",\n485\t        std::process::id(),\n486\t        tag.replace(['/', ' ', '.'], \"_\"),\n487\t        COUNTER.fetch_add(1, std::sync::atomic::Ordering::SeqCst)\n488\t    ));\n489\t    let cpath = std::ffi::CString::new(path.to_str().unwrap()).unwrap();\n490\t    unsafe {\n491\t        fflush(std::ptr::null_mut());\n492\t        let pid = fork();\n493\t        if pid == 0 {\n494\t            let fd = open(cpath.as_ptr(), O_RDWR | O_CREAT | O_TRUNC, 0o600 as c_int);\n495\t            if fd < 0 {\n496\t                _exit(120);\n497\t            }\n498\t            dup2(fd, 1);\n499\t            dup2(fd, 2);\n500\t            close(fd);\n501\t            f();\n502\t            fflush(std::ptr::null_mut());\n503\t            _exit(0);\n504\t        }\n505\t        assert!(pid > 0, \"fork failed\");\n506\t        let mut status: c_int = 0;\n507\t        waitpid(pid, &mut status, 0);\n508\t        let data = std::fs::read(&path).unwrap_or_default();\n509\t        let _ = std::fs::remove_file(&path);\n510\t        (data, status)\n511\t    }\n512\t}\n513\t\n514\tstatic COUNTER: std::sync::atomic::AtomicUsize = std::sync::atomic::AtomicUsize::new(0);\n515\t\n516\t/// Run the same closure against the C API and the Rust API in separate\n517\t/// processes and assert that output bytes and exit status are identical.\n518\tpub fn diff<F: Fn(&Api)>(tag: &str, f: F) {\n519\t    let l = libs();\n520\t    let (oc, sc) = capture(&format!(\"c_{}\", tag), || f(&l.c));\n521\t    let (or, sr) = capture(&format!(\"r_{}\", tag), || f(&l.r));\n522\t    if oc != or || sc != sr {\n523\t        let sc_ = decode_status(sc);\n524\t        let sr_ = decode_status(sr);\n525\t        let a = String::from_utf8_lossy(&oc);\n526\t        let b = String::from_utf8_lossy(&or);\n527\t        let mut msg = format!(\n528\t            \"DIVERGENCE in `{}`\\n  C status: {}\\n  R status: {}\\n\",\n529\t            tag, sc_, sr_\n530\t        );\n531\t        let al: Vec<&str> = a.lines().collect();\n532\t        let bl: Vec<&str> = b.lines().collect();\n533\t        let mut shown = 0;\n534\t        for i in 0..al.len().max(bl.len()) {\n535\t            let x = al.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(\"<missing>\");\n536\t            let y = bl.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(\"<missing>\");\n537\t            if x != y {\n538\t                msg += &format!(\"  line {}:\\n    C: {}\\n    R: {}\\n\", i + 1, x, y);\n539\t                shown += 1;\n540\t                if shown >= 12 {\n541\t                    msg += \"  ...\\n\";\n542\t                    break;\n543\t                }\n544\t            }\n545\t        }\n546\t        if shown == 0 && oc != or {\n547\t            msg += &format!(\"  bytes differ (C {} bytes, R {} bytes)\\n\", oc.len(), or.len());\n548\t        }\n549\t        panic!(\"{}\", msg);\n550\t    }\n551\t}\n552\t\n553\tpub fn decode_status(s: c_int) -> String {\n554\t    if s & 0x7f == 0 {\n555\t        format!(\"exit {}\", (s >> 8) & 0xff)\n556\t    } else {\n557\t        format!(\"signal {}\", s & 0x7f)\n558\t    }\n559\t}\n560\t\n561\t/* --- printing helpers (libc, so bytes match the library's own output) ----- */\n562\t\n563\tpub fn cs(s: &str) -> std::ffi::CString {\n564\t    std::ffi::CString::new(s).unwrap()\n565\t}\n566\t\n567\tpub unsafe fn p_str(label: &str, s: *const c_char) {\n568\t    let l = cs(label);\n569\t    if s.is_null() {\n570\t        printf(cs(\"%s=<null>\\n\").as_ptr(), l.as_ptr());\n571\t    } else {\n572\t        printf(cs(\"%s=%s\\n\").as_ptr(), l.as_ptr(), s);\n573\t    }\n574\t}\n575\t\n576\tpub unsafe fn p_int(label: &str, v: c_int) {\n577\t    printf(cs(\"%s=%d\\n\").as_ptr(), cs(label).as_ptr(), v);\n578\t}\n579\t\n580\tpub unsafe fn p_uint(label: &str, v: c_uint) {\n581\t    printf(cs(\"%s=%u\\n\").as_ptr(), cs(label).as_ptr(), v);\n582\t}\n583\t\n584\tpub unsafe fn p_num(label: &str, v: f64) {\n585\t    printf(cs(\"%s=%.17g\\n\").as_ptr(), cs(label).as_ptr(), v);\n586\t}\n587\t\n588\tpub unsafe fn p_line(s: &str) {\n589\t    puts(cs(s).as_ptr());\n590\t}\n591\t\n592\tpub unsafe fn p_ptr_nonnull(label: &str, p: *const c_void) {\n593\t    printf(cs(\"%s=%s\\n\").as_ptr(), cs(label).as_ptr(),\n594\t        cs(if p.is_null() { \"null\" } else { \"nonnull\" }).as_ptr());\n595\t}\n596\t\n597\t/* --- convenience: fresh state with builtins ------------------------------ */\n598\t\n599\tpub unsafe fn newstate(api: &Api, flags: c_int) -> JS {\n600\t    let J = (api.js_newstate)(None, std::ptr::null_mut(), flags);\n601\t    assert!(!J.is_null());\n602\t    J\n603\t}\n604\t\n605\t/// Deterministic xorshift PRNG so both runs see identical inputs.\n606\tpub struct Rng(pub u64);\n607\t\n608\timpl Rng {\n609\t    pub fn new(seed: u64) -> Rng {\n610\t        Rng(seed | 1)\n611\t    }\n612\t    pub fn next_u64(&mut self) -> u64 {\n613\t        let mut x = self.0;\n614\t        x ^= x << 13;\n615\t        x ^= x >> 7;\n616\t        x ^= x << 17;\n617\t        self.0 = x;\n618\t        x\n619\t    }\n620\t    pub fn next_u32(&mut self) -> u32 {\n621\t        (self.next_u64() >> 32) as u32\n622\t    }\n623\t    /// Random double covering the whole bit pattern space (incl. NaN/Inf).\n624\t    pub fn bits_f64(&mut self) -> f64 {\n625\t        f64::from_bits(self.next_u64())\n626\t    }\n627\t    /// \"Reasonable\" random double in a wide but finite range.\n628\t    pub fn nice_f64(&mut self) -> f64 {\n629\t        let m = (self.next_u64() >> 11) as f64 / (1u64 << 53) as f64;\n630\t        let e = (self.next_u32() % 60) as i32 - 30;\n631\t        let s = if self.next_u32() & 1 == 0 { 1.0 } else { -1.0 };\n632\t        s * m * 10f64.powi(e)\n633\t    }\n634\t    pub fn range(&mut self, n: u32) -> u32 {\n635\t        self.next_u32() % n\n636\t    }\n637\t}\n638\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01E8ecAiGGHYTpr8UWXCrPR2","session_id":"5c8219bc-b0e9-40a9-995a-ed544487508c","uuid":"f1267f0f-0c3a-4c75-a5ef-62cf70cd2cd9","timestamp":"2026-09-08T16:52:08.394Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write script corpus + builtin tests"}
