{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_cgtqyjfydmrmqtj2efltttw2rnvewqw742imiczott73x2ukmoka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_015AXznQvtuK5x3ghBX1NJEE","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Error tests rows 1-64","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are writing ONE Rust integration test file of ERROR-PATH differential tests for a C-to-Rust verification project.\n\nWorking dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-dNzXE1\n- `c_src/` = original C (MuJS 1.3.8). READ ONLY, never modify.\n- `translation/` = Rust cdylib translation. You may ONLY create/edit `translation/tests/errors_1.rs`.\n- Do NOT modify translation/src/**, Cargo.toml, tests/common/mod.rs, translation/ERRORS.md, CONFIGS.md, SYMBOLS.md, or c_src/.\n\nREAD FIRST:\n1. `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` — the harness. `diff(tag, |api| ...)` runs your closure against the C .so and the Rust .so in separate forked children with stdout+stderr captured, and asserts the captured bytes AND the exit status are identical. Helpers: `p_int`, `p_uint`, `p_num`, `p_str`, `p_line`, `p_ptr_nonnull`, `cs(\"...\")`, `newstate(api, flags)`, `Rng`, constants (JS_STRICT, JS_READONLY, ...). Api fn-pointer field signatures are in the `api!{...}` block.\n2. `translation/ERRORS.md` — the error-surface table. YOUR ROWS ARE **1 through 64** (jsarray.c, jsboolean.c, jsbuiltin.c, jscompile.c, jsdate.c, jsdtoa.c, jserror.c, jsfunction.c, jsintern.c). Each row gives the function, the C file:line, the guarding condition, and the expected error.\n3. The C source at the cited file:line, to work out what input actually reaches that branch.\n\nWHAT TO WRITE: one `#[test] fn errNNN_<short_name>()` per ERRORS.md row (err001..err064), each calling `diff(...)` with a closure that constructs EXACTLY that invalid input/condition and prints the observable result. The assertion is that C and Rust reject identically — the harness gives you that for free, so your job is to make the rejection observable and to actually hit the branch.\n\nHow to make a rejection observable:\n- For errors reachable from JavaScript (most of these): run a snippet with `js_dostring` inside a try/catch that prints the error's `name` and `message`, e.g. source\n  `try { <trigger> } catch (e) { print(e.name + \": \" + e.message) }`\n  AND also run the raw `<trigger>` through `js_dostring` without the catch and print the returned code, so the default report output (stderr) is compared too. You need a `print` global: install one with `js_newcfunction` + `js_setglobal` (use the `static mut CUR: *const Api` trick to give the callback access to the Api — set `CUR = api as *const Api;` at the top of each closure; see `dtest/driver.c` for the C version of such a print function).\n- For errors reachable only through the C API: call the C API function directly with the invalid input and print what comes back (return code, or, for functions that throw, let the child die — the harness compares exit status, so identical aborts/exits pass).\n- For rows 57 and 58 (`assert` in `minus`, jsdtoa.c): the C library is built WITH assertions, so a failing assert aborts with SIGABRT. Call `js_grisu2` with an input that hits it (`0.0` is known to abort in C). Both libraries must abort the same way; do not work around it.\n- If a row is genuinely unreachable from outside the library (e.g. an out-of-memory-only path), write the test for the CLOSEST reachable trigger and add a comment `// row N: only reachable under allocation failure; nearest reachable trigger is ...`. Never delete a row's test.\n\nVerify with: `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-dNzXE1/translation && timeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test errors_1 -- --test-threads=1 2>&1 | tail -60`\n\nEvery test must actually EXERCISE its branch — sanity check by confirming the printed error message matches the message in the ERRORS.md row (if it does not, your trigger reaches a different check; fix the trigger). Print the row number in the output of each test so it is traceable.\n\nIf a test reveals a DIVERGENCE between C and Rust, do NOT fix translation/src — keep the failing test and report the exact divergence.\n\nFINAL REPORT (concise): a list `row N: pass|fail|unreachable-proxy` for all 64 rows, then the exact diverging output for any failures."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1939,"cache_read_input_tokens":154014,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1939,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c8219bc-b0e9-40a9-995a-ed544487508c","uuid":"8882f97f-b2d1-4c9b-9ed3-051b2099aa91","timestamp":"2026-09-08T16:52:43.776Z"}
