{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_cgtqyjfydmrmqtj2efltttw2rnvewqw742imiczott73x2ukmoka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01Y8jg8CkNkGF9JhujtU4SRX","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Error tests rows 121-190","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are writing ONE Rust integration test file of ERROR-PATH differential tests for a C-to-Rust verification project.\n\nWorking dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-dNzXE1\n- `c_src/` = original C (MuJS 1.3.8). READ ONLY, never modify.\n- `translation/` = Rust cdylib translation. You may ONLY create/edit `translation/tests/errors_3.rs`.\n- Do NOT modify translation/src/**, Cargo.toml, tests/common/mod.rs, translation/ERRORS.md, CONFIGS.md, SYMBOLS.md, or c_src/.\n\nREAD FIRST:\n1. `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` — the harness. `diff(tag, |api| ...)` runs your closure against the C .so and the Rust .so in separate forked children with stdout+stderr captured and asserts captured bytes AND exit status are identical. Helpers: `p_int`, `p_uint`, `p_num`, `p_str`, `p_line`, `p_ptr_nonnull`, `cs(\"...\")`, `newstate(api, flags)`, `Rng`, constants. Api fn-pointer signatures are in the `api!{...}` block.\n2. `translation/ERRORS.md` — the error-surface table. YOUR ROWS ARE **121 through 190** (json.c, jsparse.c, jsproperty.c, jsregexp.c, jsrun.c, jsstate.c, jsstring.c, jsvalue.c).\n3. The C source at the cited file:line to work out the exact input that reaches that branch.\n\nWHAT TO WRITE: one `#[test] fn errNNN_<short_name>()` per ERRORS.md row (err121..err190), each calling `diff(...)` with a closure constructing EXACTLY that invalid input and printing the observable result.\n\nGuidance:\n- Most rows are reachable from JavaScript: run a snippet through `js_dostring` inside `try { <trigger> } catch (e) { print(e.name + \": \" + e.message) }` AND the raw snippet without the catch (so the default report output is compared