5 cflags through a counting allocator (alloc/realloc/free/free(NULL)/live counts + ctx pass-through printed after compile, exec and free); plus a NULL-after-N allocator over `fail_at` 0..5 that reproduces all four paths — \"cannot allocate regular expression\", \"... parse list\", \"... instruction list\", \"... character class list\" — with identical allocation traces; plus `regfreex(NULL)` and `errorp == NULL`.\n- **cfg53_newregexp** — 17 patterns × flags {0..7, 255, -1, 8}; `js_isregexp`/`js_isobject`/`js_iscallable`/`js_toregexp`/`js_typeof`/`js_repr`/`js_tostring` and `source`/`global`/`ignoreCase`/`multiline`/`lastIndex`/absent props; plus `js_isregexp` on 6 non-regexps and a JS `new RegExp` script covering 10 invalid patterns and flag validation. 3023 lines.\n- **cfg53_newregexp_invalid_throws** — direct `js_newregexp(\"(a*)*\")` with a `js_atpanic` handler: both libs reach the panic and exit 9 with the same output.\n- **cfg54_regexp_prototype_exec** — 14 (pattern, text) cases × 7 flag combos, iterating `js_RegExp_prototype_exec` until null (6 iterations when global) printing len/index/input/every capture and `lastIndex` after each call, plus the `lastIndex > strlen` reset path. 851 lines.\n- **cfg54_regexp_from_js** — `/re/g.exec` loop, `test`, `replace` (string, `$1 $& $\\` $' $$`, function), `match`, `split`, `search`, `m`/`i` flags, UTF-8 index, empty-match advance.\n\nTwo implementation notes worth keeping in mind for other tests: `js_tostring(J, idx)` on an object **replaces the stack slot** with the primitive (so regexp properties must be read before, or via `js_copy`), and `newstate()` does not install `print`, so the JS scripts accumulate into a global `OUT` string that is read back and printed (with `fflush` around `js_dostring` so stdout/stderr interleaving stays deterministic)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":981,"cache_read_input_tokens":156549,"cache_creation"