>t.type = JS_TOBJECT`). GCC evaluates the arguments right-to-left, so C computes `transient = 1` *before* boxing; Rust guarantees left-to-right evaluation, so `js_toobject` boxes the slot first and `js_isobject` then returns 1, giving `transient = 0`. Exact diff (strict state, cfunction pushes `\"abc\"` + `1` then calls `js_setproperty(J, -2, \"zzz\")`):\n```\nC: TypeError: cannot create property 'zzz' on transient object   /  raw: rc=1\nR: no error                                                      /  raw: rc=0\n```\n(Note: this is the *only* way to reach that branch — `OP_SETPROP`/`OP_SETPROP_S` compute `obj` before `transient` explicitly, so `transient` is always 0 there. The test also shows the JS path silently succeeding in both libraries.)\n\n**row 135 — `jsV_resizearray` (jsproperty.c:325) `assert(!obj->u.a.simple)`: abort message missing in Rust.**\nBoth abort with SIGABRT (status matches), but the C library's glibc `assert` writes a message to stderr that the Rust `abort()` does not:\n```\nC: <exe>: .../c_src/src/jsproperty.c:325: jsV_resizearray: Assertion `!obj->u.a.simple' failed.\nR: <missing>\n```\n(`translation/src/jsproperty.rs:417` is `if (*obj).u.a.simple != 0 { abort(); }` — bare abort, no `__assert_fail` text. Same pattern likely affects every other C `assert` in the crate.)\n\n### Unreachable rows (nearest reachable trigger tested instead, documented in-file)\n- **153 / 154 / 156** — asserts in the `static` `jsR_setarrayindex`; both callers already guarantee `simple`, `k >= 0` and `newlen <= flat_length+1`. Flat-array fast paths exercised instead.\n- **155** — the `newlen > JS_ARRAYLIMIT` check inside `jsR_setarrayindex` needs `flat_length >= 1<<26`, i.e. a 1 GiB flat array; the identical \"array too large\" check on `a.length` is covered by row 158.\n- **169** — `delete <identifier>` is rejected at compile time in strict mode (`jscompile.c cdelete`) and `J->strict` always mirrors the running function's strict flag, so `js_delvar` can never see `J->strict != 0`. Test shows the compile-time rejection plus the silent non-strict path.\n- **175** — `OP_GETLOCAL` is only emitted for names in the function's own `vartab`, all of which `jsR_callfunction` `js_initvar()`s first. Test uses the identical message from `OP_GETVAR` inside a non-lightweight function.\n- **178 / 179** — `assert(sizeof(js_Value)==16)` / `assert(soffsetof(...)==15)` are compile-time layout properties. Instead these tests cover the reachable jsstate.c error paths: `js_ploadstring` returning 1, the `JS_TRYLIMIT`=64 `js_ptry` path (63 nested JS `try`s then a cfunction calling `js_ploadstring` → rc=1, `\"exception stack overflow\"`), and `js_pcall`/`js_pconstruct` returning 1.\n\nNotable interpreter-limit rows that do pass: 170 `call stack overflow` (1024-deep JS recursion, `jsR_pushtrace` wins over `jsR_savescope`), 174 `js_endtry` with no try frame → `uncaught exception` + SIGABRT, 137/138/180 `regexec failed` via `/a*b/` on 8192 `a`s (REG_MAXREC=4096), 144/145/184/185 the `JS_STRLIMIT` (1<<28) paths using real 256 MiB buffers plus the `js_pushliteral` no-check trick."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":288,"cache_read_input_tokens":181596,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":288,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Y8jg8CkNkGF9JhujtU4SRX","session_id":"5c8219bc-b0e9-40a9-995a-ed544487508c","uuid":"35b7424e-9706-44ef-b70b-8ddc3fbe3de2","timestamp":"2026-09-08T17:13:06.843Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Error tests rows 121-190"}
