{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_eny7wwbg7xwpex6xrxfhykkpdm5p3x7hbyauv5fbuayf3twriq2q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Wrote `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-dNzXE1/translation/tests/scripts.rs` (1278 lines, 8 tests). Total runtime **47 s**. Result: **7 pass, 1 fail (cfg89 — real divergence)**.\n\n## Per-test results\n\n| test | row | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cfg57_corpus_nonstrict` | 57 | **pass** — all 206 `dtest/js/*.js` through `js_dostring`, non-strict |\n| `cfg58_corpus_strict` | 58 | **pass** — same corpus with `JS_STRICT` |\n| `cfg89_drivers` | 89 | **FAIL** — 1 of 58 direct driver comparisons diverges (+ `run.sh`'s 485) |\n| `cfg90_date` | 90 | **pass** — 1236 output lines × TZ ∈ {UTC, America/New_York, Asia/Kolkata} |\n| `cfg91_json` | 91 | **pass** — 2382 lines incl. 200 fixed-seed random JSON docs |\n| `cfg92_math` | 92 | **pass** — 1585 lines, 500 random doubles + specials |\n| `cfg93_string` | 93 | **pass** — 5287 lines, 200 random strings |\n| `cfg94_array` | 94 | **pass** — 4918 lines, 100 random arrays |\n\n## The divergence (cfg89, mode `-lowlevel`)\n\nInput: `driver_c -lowlevel` / `driver_r -lowlevel`, at the first `js_grisu2(0.0, buf, &K)` call (`nums[0] == 0` in `lowleveltest`). Both abort with **signal 6** and byte-identical 25320-byte stdout (last line `rune 750: a=1 l=0 u=0 lower=750 upper=750`). Only stderr differs:\n\n```\nC: driver_c: .../c_src/src/jsdtoa.c:387: minus: Assertion `x.f >= y.f' failed.\nR: <missing>          (no output at all)\n```\n\nCause: `translation/src/jsdtoa.rs` translated `assert(x.f >= y.f)` (and `assert(x.e == y.e)`) as a bare `abort()` (lines 266 / 270, with the asserts left as comments on 264 / 268), so glibc's `__assert_fail` diagnostic is lost. `dtest/run.sh` reports the same single `OUTPUT DIFF lowlevel` out of 485 comparisons. Left failing as instructed; `translation/src` untouched.\n\n## Two test-harness traps found and fixed (worth knowing)\n\n1. **`LD_LIBRARY_PATH` made driver comparisons vacuous.** `c_src/build/libmujs.so` has `SONAME libmujs.so`, so `driver_c` records `NEEDED libmujs.so`, which the loader resolves via `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` *before* the `-Wl,-rpath` RUNPATH. `cargo test` puts `target/release` on `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`, so `driver_c` silently loaded the **Rust** library and every comparison (including `bash run.sh` spawned from the test) passed trivially. Fixed by pinning `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` per child (`c_src/build` for `driver_c`, `target/release` for `driver_r`) and `env_remove`ing it for `run.sh`. The Rust cdylib has no SONAME, so `driver_r` keeps a literal relative `NEEDED` path and must be run with cwd = `dtest`.\n2. **`js_newcfunction` does not copy the name** (`c_src/src/jsvalue.c:493` stores the pointer), so passing a temporary `CString` left a dangling pointer that surfaced as `[CFunction <garbage>]` in `t13_trap.js`. Names are now `'static` byte literals.\n\nRows 57/58 use a local `diff_norm` (byte-exact first, falling back to `0x[0-9a-f]+` → `PTR` exactly as `dtest/run.sh` does) because `t13_trap.js` prints raw object addresses (`[Function 0x1cabcb90, f, [string]:1]`) that differ between any two processes. `run.sh` itself is executed inside cfg89 (30 s, well under the 300 s limit; a `timeout 300` guard skips it otherwise).\n\nTwo behaviours worth noting, identical in both libraries so not failures: mujs has no `String.prototype.substr` (Annex B) — the tests record the identical `TypeError`; and mujs's `replace` callback omits trailing non-participating capture groups, so the replacement function inspects `arguments`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":421,"cache_read_input_tokens":187756,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":421,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01E8ec