{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_tnlch4t56l2t4oybofuavoc75jy5aeypvjsitocczjs3lluc57fa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 19 tests pass. Here's the report.\n\n## Deliverable\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-dNzXE1/translation/tests/objects.rs` (only file created/edited; ~1750 lines, 21 `diff` tags, ~340 KB of byte-compared C-vs-Rust output).\n\n## Results — one `#[test]` per CONFIGS.md row\n\n| test fn | row | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cfg29_newobject_setget` | 29 | PASS |\n| `cfg30_flat_array_setindex` | 30 | PASS (n = 0,1,2,7,8,9,64,1000; 6140 lines) |\n| `cfg31_sparse_array_setindex` | 31 | PASS |\n| `cfg32_array_named_property` | 32 | PASS |\n| `cfg33_get_set_length` | 33 | PASS (incl. 100000, and RangeError paths via protected call) |\n| `cfg34_lowlevel_resize_unflatten` | 34 | PASS (see note below) |\n| `cfg35_hasindex_getindex_delindex` | 35 | PASS |\n| `cfg36_defproperty_atts` | 36 | PASS (atts 0..=7, non-strict + `JS_STRICT`) |\n| `cfg37_defaccessor` | 37 | PASS |\n| `cfg38_property_own_inherited_missing` | 38 | PASS |\n| `cfg39_lowlevel_properties` | 39 | PASS (200 `Rng::new(0xC0FFEE)` names) |\n| `cfg40_jsV_newobject_classes` | 40 | PASS (classes -1,0..16,99 × proto NULL/Object.prototype) |\n| `cfg41_pushiterator` | 41 | PASS (12 shapes × own=0/1) |\n| `cfg42_jsV_newiterator` | 42 | PASS |\n| `cfg43_globals` | 43 | PASS (non-strict + strict) |\n| `cfg44_registry` | 44 | PASS |\n| `cfg45_ref_unref` | 45 | PASS |\n| `cfg51_wrapper_objects` | 51 | PASS |\n| `cfg52_errors` | 52 | PASS (all 7 ctors × 3 messages) |\n\n**No semantic divergence was found in any of these rows.** I verified none of the passes is vacuous (a temporary QA wrapper confirmed every child exits 0 and reaches its final `topN=` marker; 44–6140 lines per tag).\n\n## One behavioural difference found (row 34, not a semantic bug)\nC `jsV_resizearray` (c_src/src/jsproperty.c:325) has `assert(!obj->u.a.simple)` and the C `.so` is built with assertions on. The Rust translation keeps the check but as a bare `abort()`:\n\n```rust\n/* assert(!obj->u.a.simple); */\nif (*obj).u.a.simple != 0 { abort(); }   // translation/src/jsproperty.rs:414-421\n```\n\nCalling it on a simple array kills both processes with **signal 6 at the same point** (neither reaches the code after the call), but the captured stderr differs:\n- C: `objects-…: /local/home/…/c_src/src/jsproperty.c:325: jsV_resizearray: Assertion '!obj->u.a.simple' failed.`\n- Rust: *(nothing)*\n\nBecause that diagnostic embeds an absolute path to the C sources it can never match, so `diff` can never pass on this case. I therefore implemented `cfg34b` with the harness's `capture()` directly: it asserts C and Rust have **identical exit status** (`signal 6`), that the lines printed *before* the call match, and that neither printed `survived`. Everything else in row 34 (`jsR_unflattenarray` on flat/already-unflattened/non-array objects, `jsV_resizearray` grow / shrink-mid / shrink-to-0 / iterator-vs-delete-loop shrink paths) goes through normal `diff` and passes.\n\n## Notes on technique\n- Exception-raising configurations (strict-mode read-only writes, non-configurable deletes, getter-only writes, invalid array lengths, `jsV_nextiterator` on a non-iterator) run inside a `js_newcfunction` trampoline invoked via `js_pcall`, so the error message and stack effect are compared instead of aborting the child. Caught messages are e.g. `TypeError: 'p' is read-only`, `TypeError: 's4' is non-configurable`, `TypeError: setting property 'acc' that only has a getter`.\n- Determinism: `js_ref` on objects returns a `%p` address, so object refs are printed only via `p_ptr_nonnull` (primitive refs `0`,`1`,`2`,`_True`,`_False`,`_Undefined`,`_Null` are printed literally). Error `stack` was checked and is safe (`Error: stackyundefined` — no paths/line numbers at top level, `tracetop == 0`).\n- `js_tostring` mutates the stack slot in place for numbers/objects, so it is only ever called on a `js_copy` when the slot must survive."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1703,"cache_read_input_tokens":180784,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1703,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01FN1FjDBBBQ8HvW4Sz4NFkA","session_id":"5c8219bc-b0e9-40a9-995a-ed544487508c","uuid":"0e037000-5196-4c88-8c8f-c48e31c6b1c7","timestamp":"2026-09-08T17:29:03.533Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write object/property tests"}
