l `topN=` marker; 44–6140 lines per tag).\n\n## One behavioural difference found (row 34, not a semantic bug)\nC `jsV_resizearray` (c_src/src/jsproperty.c:325) has `assert(!obj->u.a.simple)` and the C `.so` is built with assertions on. The Rust translation keeps the check but as a bare `abort()`:\n\n```rust\n/* assert(!obj->u.a.simple); */\nif (*obj).u.a.simple != 0 { abort(); }   // translation/src/jsproperty.rs:414-421\n```\n\nCalling it on a simple array kills both processes with **signal 6 at the same point** (neither reaches the code after the call), but the captured stderr differs:\n- C: `objects-…: /local/home/…/c_src/src/jsproperty.c:325: jsV_resizearray: Assertion '!obj->u.a.simple' failed.`\n- Rust: *(nothing)*\n\nBecause that diagnostic embeds an absolute path to the C sources it can never match, so `diff` can never pass on this case. I therefore implemented `cfg34b` with the harness's `capture()` directly: it asserts C and Rust have **identical exit status** (`signal 6`), that the lines printed *before* the call match, and that neither printed `survived`. Everything else in row 34 (`jsR_unflattenarray` on flat/already-unflattened/non-array objects, `jsV_resizearray` grow / shrink-mid / shrink-to-0 / iterator-vs-delete-loop shrink paths) goes through normal `diff` and passes.\n\n## Notes on technique\n- Exception-raising configurations (strict-mode read-only writes, non-configurable deletes, getter-only writes, invalid array lengths, `jsV_nextiterator` on a non-iterator) run inside a `js_newcfunction` trampoline invoked via `js_pcall`, so the error message and stack effect are compared instead of aborting the child. Caught messages are e.g. `TypeError: 'p' is read-only`, `TypeError: 's4' is non-configurable`, `TypeError: setting property 'acc' that only has a getter`.\n- Determinism: `js_ref` on objects returns a `%p` address, so object refs are printed only via `p_ptr_nonnull` (primitive refs `0`,`1`,`2`,`_True`,`_False`,`_Undefined`,`_Null` are printed literally). Error `stack` was checked and is safe (`Error: stackyundefined` — no paths/line numbers at top level, `tracetop == 0`).\n- `js_tostring` mutates the stack slot in place for numbers/objects, so it is only ever called on a `js_copy` when the slot must survive.","usage":{"total_tokens":184732,"tool_uses":76,"duration_ms":2429588},"uuid":"8b5ed139-59a4-44b3-b243-85c9dd605aa4","session_id":"5c8219bc-b0e9-40a9-995a-ed544487508c"}
