ent flag is computed *before* `js_toobject` boxes the primitive in place. Rust's left-to-right order made `transient` always 0, so the `cannot create property '%s' on transient object` TypeError never fired. Fixed; pinned by `evalorder.rs` and `errors_3.rs::err160` (verified to fail against the pre-fix code).\n2. Eight C runtime `assert()`s were missing (only comments). The C library is built with assertions live, so e.g. `js_grisu2(0.0)` aborts with SIGABRT while Rust returned normally — an exit-status divergence. All eight now abort at the identical point.\n\n**One residual difference, unmatchable by construction:** glibc's `__assert_fail` prints the program name and absolute C source path before aborting. The Rust aborts silently at the same point, so assert tests compare stdout + exit status with stderr discarded (`diff_stdout`); driver comparisons strip those lines. Documented in `ERRORS.md`.\n\nTest infrastructure hardening worth noting: `cargo test` does *not* rebuild a cdylib, so the harness now refuses to run against a `libmujs.so` older than any `src/` file — a stale library would have made every comparison vacuous (as would the `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`/`SONAME` trap in the driver comparison, also fixed)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":514,"cache_read_input_tokens":260491,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":514,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c8219bc-b0e9-40a9-995a-ed544487508c","uuid":"fe3aaabb-9b53-4b45-9016-b0928bb76606","timestamp":"2026-09-08T17:43:43.393Z"}
